   "t": 625,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp2ppbp/2np1np1/2p5/2PPP3/2N1BP2/PP2N1PP/R2QKB1R w KQ - 2 8",
   "line": [
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "It releases the tension into a Maroczy-type bind. Instead the knight to c6, keeping the tension and pressing the d-pawn, was the better path.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 630.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp2ppbp/2np1np1/2pP4/2P1P3/2N1BP2/PP2N1PP/R2QKB1R b KQ - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 644,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp2ppbp/3p1np1/2pPn3/2P1P3/2N1BP2/PP2N1PP/R2QKB1R w KQ - 1 9",
   "line": [
    "Ne5"
   ],
   "spoken": "And after d5, where does the knight go? When a central pawn advances, ask which squares weaken — here it is e5, so the knight to e5, hitting the pawn.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 648,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp2ppbp/3p1np1/2pP4/2PnP3/2N1BP2/PP2N1PP/R2QKB1R w KQ - 5 11",
